{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1286299-kuei-jin-and-hunter-the-reckoning","id":1286299,"title":"Kuei-jin and Hunter the Reckoning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-09T15:23:26-08:00","id":1286299,"title":"Kuei-jin and Hunter the Reckoning","content":"So, the Hunter Storyteller\u2019s Companion seems to draw upon Kuei-jin lore/terms in describing the origin of the Imbued, making references to the 10,000 heroes and their ability to draw upon chi. This got me thinking: is there a reason ever given as to why there are no Western Kuei-jin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T15:26:39-08:00","id":1286300,"title":"","content":"I want to say yes, but I'll be dipped if I can remember where or why.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The KotE Companion, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T01:17:53-08:00","id":1286385,"title":"","content":"It's been ages since I read it, and I'm not sure which book it was in, but if I recall, there are Western Keui-Jin but they are rare. It has to do with belief and established community. Belief in Eastern traditions, but I mean real spiritual belief gives it a chance to happen. Then should it happen, well a Kuei-Jin needs to survive in a place that at many times was hostile to their type of foreigner, all while being unaware of what they actually were now and difficult learning curve since quite possibly they'd be all alone.<br /> <br /> Now in our modern times that may have changed a bit, but it would still put a Western Kuei-Jin community at a disadvantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T02:20:22-08:00","id":1288549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trategos_Sol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1286299-kuei-jin-and-hunter-the-reckoning#post1286299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This got me thinking: is there a reason ever given as to why there are no Western Kuei-jin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes<br /> I think it was in the 1000 Hell Book, a very little line about the Yama Kings. Actually it is their &quot;fault&quot;. When they &quot;built&quot; Yomi, expanding their domain by tearing part out the Yin and Yang worlds (Umbra/Dark Umbra) and the Middle Kingdom (Material) and conducting rituals to modify thir original role as purifiers and redeemers, necessary jailors who obeyed the August Personage of Jade. (As such, they had their own pocket dimensions where they enacted their necessary, if unpleasant, duties.) so the sinners would still end up in their little Hells, they locked themselves out from the western hemispehre, but at the time they saw only &quot;barbarians&quot; there (I doubt in their eyes that changed) and not really considered that a loss. The &quot;role&quot; of Yomi was somewhat filled by Malfeas and the Maeljins in the West (the book even mentions, they have some &quot;diplomatic&quot; relationship between Yomi and Malfeas, slave caravans, gifts coming back and forth and lots of lots of smiles, and while they would gleefully tear each other apart, Malfeas is too chaotic to muster a real invasion force to attack Yomi, where in their home turf, the Yama Kings are literally Gods with armies of Demonic servants and the Yama Kings rearlly capable of working together more than 5 minutes without ploting to stab the each others in the back and annex the falle Yama King's relam to organize an attack, and even if one side would attack, the cost would be too high and overall, the whole war is pointless, the Demon Emperor and the Sixth age is coming) <br /> Since the &quot;requirments&quot; to become a Kuei-Jin is to, well, escape from Yomi, without Yomi there can't be any Western Kuei-jin^^<br /> Now where is the border of East and West? Thats a bit blurry... with infulence and culture the said border could be expanded, that is why there are some &quot;Western Kuei-Jin&quot; with the colonization and all, and Banes, cainites and other Malfeas influence popping up in the East. <br /> In the west there isn't any realm just to purifie and redeem a human soul, to toss it back to the Cycle after the punsihment... there is no &quot;Yomi&quot;<br /> Maybe there was - from this point this is my theory/headcanon mind you - lots of said things are in the western relegions/paganism&quot;, from Egypt to the North, sinners go there, good ones go there, and after a time you could ascend to higher plane. One couldimmagine, a soul or two managed to escape Tartaros or Hel or Kur or Uffern or Peklo or Xibalba just to name a few &quot;Hells&quot;, made a pact with hteir Shadow/P'o and returned to their body to Rise (*cough* like the Risen *cough*) but never managed to became that infulental like the Wen-Kuei (who basically cemented themselves in the East culture) or the local undead/shapeshifter/whatever population killed them off...<br /> ...on the other hand, almost every western culture have plenty of tales about heroes comming back from the dead to defend their people or bring hope<br /> <br /> (For example:<br /> Theseus, a great abductor of women, and his bosom companion, Pirithous, since they were sons of Zeus and Poseidon, pledged themselves to marry daughters of Zeus. Theseus, in an old tradition, chose Helen, and together they kidnapped her, intending to keep her until she was old enough to marry. Pirithous chose Persephone. They left Helen with Theseus's mother, Aethra at Aphidna, whence she was rescued by the Dioscuri.<br /> On Pirithous' behalf they travelled to the underworld, domain of Persephone and her husband Hades. As they wandered through the outskirts of Tartarus, Theseus sat down to rest on a rock. As he did so he felt his limbs change and grow stiff. He tried to rise but could not. He was fixed to the rock. As he turned to cry out to his friend, he saw that Pirithous too was crying out. Around him gathered the terrible band of Furies with snakes in their hair, torches and long whips in their hands. Before these monsters the hero's courage failed and he was led away to eternal punishment.<br /> For many months in half darkness, Theseus sat immovably fixed to the rock, mourning for both his friend and for himself. In the end he was rescued by Heracles who had come to the underworld for his 12th task. There he persuaded Persephone to forgive him for the part he had taken in the rash venture of Pirithous. So Theseus was restored to the upper air but Pirithous never left the kingdom of the dead, for when he tried to free Pirithous, the underworld shook. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T03:40:37-08:00","id":1288565,"title":"","content":"there was western kuei-jin,<br /> there's mention of kuei-jin established in the Americas that predate the Sabbat, and possibly even predate the Tlacique<br /> <br /> unfortunately, they were destroyed during the war between the Sabbat and the nahualli,<br /> as the Sabbat didn't know about the kuei-jin, they assumed they were nahualli<br /> there may have been survivors but who knows<br /> it's only in the modern nights that the sabbat learned enough about kuei-jin that they realized some of the nahualli may have been kuei-jin themselves<br /> <br /> on top of that, kuei-jin expansion is harder than cainite expansion,<br /> even if a yomi domain were to expend in the west (as is the case in modern nights with mikaboshi's domain)<br /> the resulting kuei-jin wouldn't go past the chih mei stage (equivalent of wights)<br /> <br /> Asian kuei-jin managed to make it past the chih mei stage thanks to Xue, who was active around China,<br /> and even then it took a long time for more kuei-jin to expand to the rest of Asia, Oceania and the middle east,<br /> <br /> europe is even more challenging, just look at how much trouble cainites had,<br /> for example, the only reason the Tzimisce managed to settle east europe was thanks to their antideluvian and the help of Kupala<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T03:13:17-07:00","id":1326923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1286299-kuei-jin-and-hunter-the-reckoning?p=1288565#post1288565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there was western kuei-jin,<br /> there's mention of kuei-jin established in the Americas that predate the Sabbat, and possibly even predate the Tlacique<br /> <br /> unfortunately, they were destroyed during the war between the Sabbat and the nahualli,<br /> as the Sabbat didn't know about the kuei-jin, they assumed they were nahualli<br /> there may have been survivors but who knows<br /> it's only in the modern nights that the sabbat learned enough about kuei-jin that they realized some of the nahualli may have been kuei-jin themselves<br /> <br /> on top of that, kuei-jin expansion is harder than cainite expansion,<br /> even if a yomi domain were to expend in the west (as is the case in modern nights with mikaboshi's domain)<br /> the resulting kuei-jin wouldn't go past the chih mei stage (equivalent of wights)<br /> <br /> Asian kuei-jin managed to make it past the chih mei stage thanks to Xue, who was active around China,<br /> and even then it took a long time for more kuei-jin to expand to the rest of Asia, Oceania and the middle east,<br /> <br /> europe is even more challenging, just look at how much trouble cainites had,<br /> for example, the only reason the Tzimisce managed to settle east europe was thanks to their antideluvian and the help of Kupala</div> </div> </div> </div>In what book are the Western Kuei Jin mentioned","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T11:06:46-07:00","id":1327016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1286299-kuei-jin-and-hunter-the-reckoning?p=1326923#post1326923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what book are the Western Kuei Jin mentioned</div> </div> </div> </div>Mexico City by Night<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:43:25-07:00","id":1327324,"title":"","content":"San Francisco by Night p.131 has the rules for playing a Kanbujian, Kuei-Jin who took the second breath outside of the Middle Kingdom and who has no knowledge of the Dharma\u2019s and as such cannot take one up but must create his/her own Path. They can later if instructed leave their own Path and follow a Dharma but there is no specific need for them to do so.<br /> <br /> It could even be possible for a Kanbujian to take up a western Vampiric Path or Road if s/he was found and instructed by a Cainite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}